  "rationale": "CORRECT (A) — \"Beans, groundnut paste and small dried fish such as keta school boys\". <strong>Beans, groundnut and small dried fish</strong> are among the cheapest rich protein sources in Ghanaian markets. Combining a legume with a cereal staple — beans with rice, or groundnut soup with a staple — gives a <strong>complementary amino acid pattern</strong> comparable to animal protein. Small whole dried fish add calcium and iron too.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• B — These supply sugar and energy with almost no protein, and encourage dental caries in children.\n• C — These are dilute energy foods. Thin corn porridge alone is a common cause of faltering growth after weaning.\n• D — All three are starchy energy foods with negligible protein, so the meal would remain inadequate.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — food-based dietary guidelines",
