  "rationale": "CORRECT (C) — \"Kontomire, ayoyo, garden eggs, ripe mango and fresh pawpaw\". <strong>Protective foods</strong> are the fruits and vegetables supplying vitamins, minerals and fibre, helping the body resist infection and regulate its processes. Ghanaian examples include kontomire, ayoyo, okro, garden eggs, tomato, carrot, mango, pawpaw, orange and pineapple. Dark green leaves are especially rich in iron, folate and carotene.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Oils are concentrated energy foods. Red palm oil also supplies carotene, but the group as a whole gives energy.\n• B — These are starchy staples and belong squarely in the energy-giving group.\n• D — These are animal protein foods and belong in the body-building group.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — food-based dietary guidelines",
