  "rationale": "CORRECT (B) — \"Enrich the porridge with groundnut paste, mashed beans and a little oil\". Plain corn porridge is <strong>bulky, dilute and low in protein, energy density and micronutrients</strong> — a leading cause of faltering growth after weaning in Ghana. Groundnut paste or mashed beans supply protein, and a little oil raises energy density so the child gains more nourishment from the small volume a young stomach holds.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — More of an inadequate food does not supply the missing protein and micronutrients, and a small child cannot eat enough to compensate.\n• C — Dilution lowers energy density further and is itself a direct cause of malnutrition in weaning-age children.\n• D — Tea and white bread are also low in protein, and tea additionally reduces iron absorption from the meal.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — complementary feeding guidance",
