  "rationale": "CORRECT (C) — \"Haemoglobin concentration taken from a simple finger-prick sample\". <strong>Haemoglobin</strong> is the standard field measure because it can be taken from a finger prick with a portable device, giving an immediate result at low cost. It detects anaemia, the commonest consequence of iron deficiency, though it becomes abnormal only once iron stores are already depleted.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Albumin reflects protein status and is affected by infection and liver disease. It does not measure iron.\n• B — Blood glucose screens for diabetes and says nothing about iron status or anaemia.\n• D — Sodium reflects fluid and electrolyte balance and has no relationship to iron stores.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — community nutrition surveillance",
