  "rationale": "CORRECT (A) — \"A twenty-four hour dietary recall taken during the consultation\". The <strong>twenty-four hour recall</strong> asks the patient to describe everything eaten and drunk in the preceding day. It is quick, needs no literacy or equipment, and fits inside a consultation. Its limitation is that one day may not represent usual intake, so a food frequency question is often added alongside it.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• B — A weighed record is accurate but demands literacy, scales and sustained effort, making it impractical in routine clinic work.\n• C — A food security survey assesses household access to food over time, not one individual's recent intake.\n• D — Direct observation is accurate but extremely resource intensive and alters normal eating behaviour.\n\nReference: Ghana nursing curriculum — dietary assessment",
