  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"Assess a representative sample of under-fives drawn from communities\". Estimating prevalence across a population requires a <strong>representative sample</strong> so findings can be generalised to the district. Sampling children in the community rather than at a facility avoids selection bias and captures those who never attend services, who are often the most vulnerable.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Hospital inpatients are by definition unwell and unrepresentative, so this would greatly overestimate prevalence.\n• B — Health staff children are typically better resourced and informed, so this would underestimate the true burden.\n• C — Relying on maternal concern misses children whose malnutrition has not been recognised at home.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — nutrition surveillance methods",
