  "correctChoiceId": "d",
  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"Whether he passes an appetite test by eating therapeutic food\". The <strong>appetite test</strong> is the decisive criterion. A child who willingly eats ready-to-use therapeutic food can be managed at home with weekly follow-up. Failing the appetite test indicates metabolic derangement or hidden infection and requires inpatient stabilisation, as does any medical complication or bilateral oedema.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Literacy affects how instructions are given but not clinical suitability. Counselling can be given verbally with demonstration.\n• B — Previous admission forms part of the history but does not determine the level of care needed now.\n• C — Distance is considered in planning follow-up but is not the clinical decision criterion.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — community management of acute malnutrition",
