  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"Restricting her salt intake, avoiding added salt and salted fish\". Ascites forms because sodium and water are retained. <strong>Salt restriction is the foundation of treatment</strong> and works alongside diuretics; without it the fluid returns however much diuretic is given. In Ghana the main hidden sources are salted and smoked fish, bouillon cubes and shito. Fluid restriction is added only if serum sodium falls low.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Routine protein restriction is outdated and causes muscle wasting. Cirrhotic patients need generous protein, including at bedtime.\n• B — Fat is restricted only if steatorrhoea or biliary obstruction is present. It has no effect on ascites.\n• C — The weight is retained fluid, not fat. Energy restriction would worsen the malnutrition that most cirrhotic patients already have.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — chronic liver disease; management of ascites",
  "strategy": "Match the restriction to the mechanism. Ascites is a sodium and water problem, so sodium is what you restrict. Weight that arrives in weeks is fluid, not fat.",
