  "rationale": "CORRECT (A) — \"Eat regular balanced meals and avoid the foods that trouble you personally\". Ulcers are caused mainly by <strong>Helicobacter pylori and NSAIDs</strong>, and treatment is eradication therapy plus acid suppression, not a special diet. Patients should eat regular balanced meals and avoid only those items that reliably cause them symptoms. Alcohol and smoking do delay healing and should be stopped.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• B — The milk diet is obsolete. Milk buffers acid briefly, then its calcium and protein stimulate a stronger rebound of acid secretion.\n• C — An empty stomach leaves acid unbuffered and typically worsens duodenal ulcer pain, which classically comes when hungry.\n• D — Dietary acid is trivial next to gastric acid, and excluding fruit and vegetables removes the vitamin C that supports healing.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — peptic ulcer disease",
