  "rationale": "CORRECT (C) — \"Eat about one extra small meal daily, focusing on quality of food\". Pregnancy raises energy needs only modestly — roughly <strong>one extra small meal a day</strong> in the second and third trimesters — but raises requirements for <strong>iron, folate, calcium, iodine and protein</strong> much more sharply. The counselling message is therefore about food quality and supplements rather than volume.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Doubling intake causes excessive weight gain, gestational diabetes and macrosomia. The extra requirement is far smaller.\n• B — The fetus draws on maternal stores, but if intake does not rise the mother becomes depleted, particularly of iron.\n• D — Deliberate restriction causes fetal growth restriction and does not make labour safer. It is a dangerous belief to leave uncorrected.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — antenatal care; maternal nutrition",
