  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"1650 kcal, divided between meals across the whole day\". Requirement = weight × kcal per kg, so <strong>55 × 30 = 1650 kcal daily</strong>. Sense-check: 30 kcal/kg means about 30 times the weight, and 55 × 30 sits between 55 × 20 = 1100 and 55 × 40 = 2200, so any answer outside that span must be wrong.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — 1100 kcal uses 20 kcal/kg, a maintenance figure for a patient at risk of refeeding, not the prescribed rate.\n• B — 2200 kcal uses 40 kcal/kg and would substantially overfeed this patient.\n• C — 1350 kcal does not correspond to any whole rate per kilogram and appears to come from an arithmetic slip.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — nutritional support; energy prescription",
