  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"Two sachets and a half, given in small portions through the day\". Daily energy = 175 × 8 = 1400 kcal. Sachets = <strong>1400 ÷ 500 = 2.8</strong>, which is prescribed in practice as <strong>two and a half to three sachets daily</strong>. Sense-check: each sachet covers 500 kcal, so a requirement of 1400 kcal must need between two and three sachets, ruling out the one and a half and four and a half options.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — One and a half sachets gives only 750 kcal, roughly half of what the child needs for catch-up growth.\n• B — Four and a half sachets gives 2250 kcal, far above requirement, and risks diarrhoea and refeeding problems.\n• C — Two sachets gives 1000 kcal and leaves a shortfall of 400 kcal, so weight gain would be slower than target.\n\nReference: Ghana Health Service — community management of acute malnutrition",
