  "rationale": "CORRECT (C) — \"1300 mL, given as oral fluid and feeds across the day\". The standard rule gives 100 mL/kg for the first 10 kg, then 50 mL/kg for the next 10 kg. So <strong>(10 × 100) + (6 × 50) = 1000 + 300 = 1300 mL daily</strong>. Sense-check: the answer must be more than the 1000 mL that a 10 kg child needs but well below 16 × 100 = 1600 mL, because the added kilograms count at the lower rate.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — 1600 mL applies 100 mL/kg to the whole weight and ignores that the rate falls after the first 10 kg.\n• B — 1000 mL is the allowance for the first 10 kg only and omits the remaining 6 kg entirely.\n• D — 1800 mL exceeds even the flat 100 mL/kg calculation and has no basis in the formula.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — paediatric fluid management",
