  "rationale": "CORRECT (D) — \"It shortens the episode and reduces further episodes for several months\". Zinc is lost in diarrhoeal stool and is needed for <strong>gut mucosal repair and immune function</strong>. Giving <strong>20 mg daily for 10 to 14 days</strong>, or 10 mg for infants under six months, <strong>shortens the episode and reduces recurrence over the following two to three months</strong>. It is given alongside oral rehydration solution and continued feeding.\n\nWhy the other options fail:\n• A — Zinc is not an antidiarrhoeal and has no immediate effect. Its benefit builds over the course of the treatment.\n• B — Sodium replacement is the job of oral rehydration solution. Zinc is a trace element given for repair, not for volume.\n• C — Zinc has no established role in preventing milk allergy, which is an unrelated immunological condition.\n\nReference: Ghana STG — diarrhoeal disease; zinc supplementation",
  "strategy": "Remember the three-part diarrhoea package and what each part does: fluid replaces losses, zinc repairs the gut, feeding prevents malnutrition.",
